{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they exchanged their glory</b> — a designation for the glory of HaShem, in the manner of <i>כי נאץ נאצת</i> (for you have utterly scorned), and the designation is directed against King David by way of rebuke, and he did not say to him: <i>כי נאץ נאצת השם</i> (for you have utterly scorned HaShem). Let them be a laughingstock." "<b>And the meaning of eating grass</b> — a way of disgrace and shame."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 106, :notes {0 "The last phrase 'ילעגו למו' (let them be a laughingstock) is syntactically disconnected from the preceding argument; translated hyper-literally as it stands in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:44.667049637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}